        # If opponent is White (is_white=False, we check black's attack on white? No, is_white=True means we check if white is in check, so attacked by black).
        # If is_white=True (white to move), we check if white's square is attacked by black.
        # Black pawns are at r-1? No, black pawns move +1. So a black pawn at (r-1, c) attacks (r, c) if it captures diagonally.
        # Black pawn at (r-1, c-1) captures (r, c) (down-right). Black pawn at (r-1, c+1) captures (r, c) (down-left).

